.Dd September 25, 2026
.Dt ZHACK 8
.Os
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm zhack
.Nd libzpool debugging tool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl c Ar cachefile
.Op Fl d Ar dir
.Op Fl o Ar var Ns = Ns Ar value
.Op Fl G
.Ar subcommand Op Ar arguments
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a debugging tool that performs low-level, unsupported modifications to a ZFS
storage pool using the userspace
.Sy libzpool
implementation.
It is intended for developers and for recovery of otherwise-unimportable pools.
.Pp
.Sy Most subcommands write directly to on-disk structures with little or no
.Sy validation and can irreversibly corrupt a pool .
Use them only on pools whose data is disposable or already backed up.
.
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-o var=value"
.It Fl c Ar cachefile
Read the pool configuration from the given
.Ar cachefile .
.It Fl d Ar dir
Search
.Ar dir
for the pool's vdevs when importing
.Pq may be given more than once .
.It Fl o Ar var Ns = Ns Ar value
Set the libzpool tunable
.Ar var
to the unsigned 32-bit integer
.Ar value .
.It Fl G
Dump the
.Sy zfs_dbgmsg
buffer to standard error before exiting.
.El
.
.Sh SUBCOMMANDS
.Ss General
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm feature stat
.Ar pool
.Xc
Print information about the features enabled on
.Ar pool .
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm feature enable
.Op Fl r
.Op Fl d Ar description
.Ar pool Ar feature
.Xc
Add
.Ar feature
.Pq a feature GUID
to the pool's enabled features.
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm feature ref
.Op Fl md
.Ar pool Ar feature
.Xc
Change the reference count of
.Ar feature .
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm label repair
.Op Fl cu
.Ar device
.Xc
Repair the labels of
.Ar device .
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm metaslab leak
.Ar pool
.Xc
Apply an allocation map produced by
.Xr zdb 8
to
.Ar pool .
.El
.
.Ss RAIDZ parity-reshape toolkit
These subcommands implement the offline, crash-resumable primitives used by
.Xr zpool-reparity 8
to reshape a RAIDZ pool's parity level in place, and by the accompanying
verifiers.
They operate on an exported pool imported through
.Nm .
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm raidz_epochs
.Ar pool Ar top-vdev-id Ar start : Ns Ar width : Ns Ar parity Ns ...
.Xc
Write the RAIDZ parity-epoch table
.Pq one or more Ar start : Ns Ar width : Ns Ar parity No tuples
to the top-level vdev's ZAP verbatim and activate the
.Sy raidz_parity_epochs
feature.
No validation is performed, so damaged tables can be injected for testing;
disposable pools only.
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm reparity
.Ar pool
.Xc
Sweep the Meta Object Set, re-encoding pool metadata at the parity level
declared by the current epoch table.
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm reparity_commit
.Ar pool Ar vdev_guid
.Xc
Census the vdev and, if every reachable block conforms to the target parity,
write the commit marker that finalizes the reshape.
Refuses
.Pq fail-closed
if any block does not conform.
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm reparity_commit_raw
.Ar pool Ar vdev_guid Ar parity Ar completion Ar digest
.Xc
Write a commit marker with the supplied fields directly, bypassing the census.
For testing the reconstruction path's response to a forged or inconsistent
marker; never use on a real pool.
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm normalize_verify
.Ar pool Ar checksum-name Ar compress-name
.Xc
Verify that every file-data block conforms to the given checksum and
compression, failing closed on any traversal error.
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm placement_verify
.Ar pool Ar excluded_vdev_id
.Xc
Verify that no file-data block is placed on the excluded vdev, failing closed
on any traversal error.
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm snap_bpr
.Ar pool Op Ar snapshot
.Xc
Rewrite block pointers so that snapshot-referenced blocks are re-encoded at the
new parity level while preserving their logical birth times, allowing a reshape
to complete without destroying snapshots.
With no
.Ar snapshot ,
all snapshots are processed.
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm snap_repoint
.Ar pool Ar snapshot Ar dataset
.Xc
Repoint
.Ar snapshot
at the given source
.Ar dataset .
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm snap_reanchor
.Ar pool Ar snapshot Ar creation_txg Op Ar prev_snap_txg
.Xc
Rewrite a snapshot's creation transaction group
.Pq and optionally its predecessor's
in the snapshot chain.
.It Xo
.Nm
.Cm raidz_contract
.Ar pool Ar vdev_guid Ar target_width Ar dataset Ns ...
.Xc
Reduce the logical width of a RAIDZ top-level vdev to
.Ar target_width ,
reflowing the affected datasets.
.El
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zdb 8 ,
.Xr zpool-reparity 8 ,
.Xr zpool-features 7
